WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.807
Change management goes beyond syntax.

00:00:02.807 --> 00:00:09.027
A CREATE OR REPLACE command may succeed, but a semantic change can still break analytics.

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:15.452
Consumers may depend on a column name, data type, business definition, or row grain.

00:00:15.452 --> 00:00:19.832
Review those contract elements before changing a shared object.

00:00:19.832 --> 00:00:23.432
Reusable SQL objects create dependencies.

00:00:23.432 --> 00:00:30.437
Before changing a base view, identify which other views, reports, or applications depend on it.

00:00:30.437 --> 00:00:33.877
Good change management includes version awareness, tests,

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:39.078
and communication—not just editing CREATE VIEW until it succeeds.
